'''''Arthrostemma ciliatum''''', commonly known as '''pinkfringe''', is a species of flowering [[plant]] native to the tropical Americas.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |last=Kinsey |first=T. Beth |title=Arthrostemma ciliatum – Pinkfringe |url=https://wildlifeofhawaii.com/flowers/1215/arthrostemma-ciliatum-pinkfringe/ |access-date=February 3, 2026 |website=Hawaiian Plants and Tropical Flowers}}</ref>

==Description==
''Arthrostemma ciliatum'' is an herb with a sprawling habit that can extend {{convert|1|to|4|m|ft}}.<ref name=":0" /> It has reddish stems and red buds that develop into pink or purple flowers with prominent [[stamen]]s.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |title=Arthrostemma ciliatum |url=https://www.orchidbotanics.co.uk/product-page/arthrostemma-ciliatum |access-date=February 3, 2026 |website=Orchid Botanics}}</ref> The leaves are [[Ovate (botany)|ovate]] to [[lanceolate]] and edged with tiny, bristly-hairy, reddish teeth. 

==Ecology==
The pinkfringe is perennial, and grows aggressively along riverbanks, in humid forests, and in disturbed areas.<ref name=":1" /> It can be found at middle elevations from {{convert|500|to|1000|m|mi}} across the [[Greater Antilles]], [[Mexico]], and [[Central America|Central]] and [[South America]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Arthrostemma ciliatum Fragile pinkfringe |url=https://www.regionalconservation.org/ircs/database/plants/PlantPagePR.asp?TXCODE=Arthcili |access-date=February 3, 2026 |website=Plants of the Island of Puerto Rico}}</ref> The pinkfringe has also naturalized in [[Hawaii]], where it is considered a weed.<ref name=":0" /><ref name=":1" /> 

==Uses==
The pinkfringe is a popular ornamental plant.<ref name=":1" /> It also has tender, edible stems, which can be used for food. Medicinally, it has been used to treat a variety of conditions, from [[diabetes]]<nowiki/>to [[urinary tract infection]]s and [[sexually transmitted infection]]s.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Pinkfringe |url=https://theark.green/producto/pinkfringe/ |access-date=February 3, 2026 |website=The Green Ark Foundation}}</ref> 

